tu Note on other languages

t2 C

p Originally, the ZPL was supposed to be a kind of tiny project. \
It wasn't even necessarily a language. The history behind this is quite simple :

p Actually I saw that people around me and on the internet thought that \
the C programming language was hard to learn and requires too much rigour and harsh training to use it. \
When needing to do a tiny little script quickly, the C wasn't even an option : "leave it !"

p For "little task" usage, use Python or Shell scripts instead. \
In less than 50 lines, you do more than hundreds of lines of C code, \
and you don't have to create all of the basic tools for manipulating strings or any complex structure.



