t2 C++

p For me, there is mostly one reason explaining the poor number of tools available in C standard libraries and its name is C++. \
I clearly don't understand why people has been so interested in such a language. \
Every time I think about it, a short circuit occurs in in my head. \
Nobody even tried to do something better that the existing ?

p Am I the only one considerating that there is A WAY TOO MUCH things to manage data ? \
Am I the only one who finds it too COMPLICATED for beginners ? \
"C++ is too big to be melted again. Don't waste time in re-inventing the wheel."

p Hmm... Alright. But I am not afraid of this giant. \
I am a believer so I believe I can do a performance-similar language that can either suits to beginners, \
high-level programmers and low-level programmers.

p The only reason I could ever find to explain this passion is that it is the only language that offers lots of \
useful libraries AND that is close enough to a C code. \
There are also some practical shortcuts in bonus and that's great, I do not condemn that however, \
too much things are so complicated... Too bad.




